  "title": "NAND vs NOR Universal Gate Implementation Comparison",
  "description": "Implement the Boolean function F = (A + B)(C + D) in two separate ways. First, implement it strictly using only 3-input NOR gates from a single 7427 IC. Second, implement the same function strictly using only 2-input NAND gates from 7400 ICs. Both implementations must produce identical outputs for every input combination. Connect A, B, C, and D to SW0, SW1, SW2, and SW3 respectively. Route the NOR implementation output F_NOR to LED0 and the NAND implementation output F_NAND to LED1.",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "design",
